  "content_description": "",
  "content_text_body": "Compassionate teams tend to be less stressed, more engaged, and better connected. The objective is to practice compassion in creating a team climate where everyone is comfortable being themselves.\n\n### Listen actively\nThe goal of active listening is to truly hear and understand where the other person is coming from. Don't try to offer solutions or fill silences. Rather, ask questions that help you better understand the thoughts and feelings of the other person.\n\n### Provide support\nWhen you feel you fully understand the other person, offer resources or support that you think might be helpful. Don't push these on the person. Instead, empower them to pursue the types of support that feel right to them.\n\nRead [How to Be Successful and Still Compassionate](https://greatergood.berkeley.edu/article/item/how_to_be_successful_and_still_compassionate/) for more advice.",
